WEBVTT

00:00:03.170 --> 00:00:04.230
T-that can't be!

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:07.800
There's not even a single
craft in the planet's vicinity!

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:09.070
Impossible!

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:12.710
There's supposed to be a huge,
100,000-ship exercise at Bregma!

00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:15.750
But there really is nobody out there!

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:18.080
We're the only ones here!

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:20.520
W-why is the fleet-

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.020
This means that we're-

00:00:23.020 --> 00:00:25.290
A message from an unmanned Bregma base!

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:27.960
It's from the Union's
Exercise Management Division!

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.730
It's a Level 1 coded message!

00:00:29.730 --> 00:00:32.230
Okay! Decipher it at once!

00:00:32.230 --> 00:00:35.760
Medical and technology instructors
to the conference room!

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:40.700
We've learned that the Deague
is planning an assault

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:43.240
with a million-ship armada.

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:45.110
That's of an incredible scale!

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:47.810
The largest in history.

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:50.710
These are the enemy's
estimated staging posts.

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:54.520
In response to this, the Union decided
to intercept them here,

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:56.520
and notified all fleets.

00:00:56.520 --> 00:00:59.390
It appears the general forces
at Bregma ceased their exercises

00:00:59.390 --> 00:01:01.290
and headed for an intercept point as well.

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:04.230
That explains why there's not a soul here...

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:06.830
Looks like our only choice
is to head back to Basion,

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:09.700
without new supplies or repairs...

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:13.240
But it's not all bad.

00:01:13.240 --> 00:01:17.070
The enemy's trying to devote every
ship in the area for this mission.

00:01:17.070 --> 00:01:19.910
Every ship? Does that mean-

00:01:19.910 --> 00:01:21.580
Yes.

00:01:21.580 --> 00:01:26.610
We can safely assume the guys
chasing us were sent away, too!

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:32.570
The Beginning of Revelry

00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:42.550
How could we have done
something so unforgivable?

00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:46.660
How can I atone for this? How?!

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:50.230
You can atone...

00:01:50.230 --> 00:01:54.060
If I open the Baxter Gate inside me...

00:02:03.940 --> 00:02:06.040
Are you all right?

00:02:06.040 --> 00:02:06.880
What-

00:02:06.880 --> 00:02:10.610
Your mental load suddenly increased
while you were linked to her

00:02:10.610 --> 00:02:12.310
and you blacked out.

00:02:12.310 --> 00:02:15.010
Emily's just fine, don't worry.

00:02:16.320 --> 00:02:18.650
That... wasn't a dream...

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:22.090
It all really happened...

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:24.590
D-do you hurt anywhere?

00:02:24.590 --> 00:02:26.300
No, I'm fine...

00:02:26.300 --> 00:02:28.860
Great! Then let's restart the experiment!

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:32.570
We need to investigate the cause
of what happened back there, too!

00:02:32.570 --> 00:02:36.140
I thought I was being handed
over to the military?

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:38.940
That's on hold for a while.

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:42.680
How anti-climactic!

00:02:42.680 --> 00:02:45.150
We struggle so hard to reach Bregma,

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:49.150
and we find no one's here to help
and no one's chasing us anymore...

00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:51.220
Are we sure they're not coming?

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:53.160
Given the time limit,

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:58.290
they had to have gone straight to
the staging point from Gall space...

00:02:58.290 --> 00:02:59.930
Oh...

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:02.230
My brother will come!

00:03:02.230 --> 00:03:06.070
Come on, now! They're staging
an incredibly massive operation!

00:03:06.070 --> 00:03:08.300
Just because he's Ralph Werec-

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:10.240
No, because he is a traitor,

00:03:10.240 --> 00:03:12.940
they'd never allow him to act
on his own at a time like this!

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:15.140
He can't come, even if he wants to!

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:17.780
He'll still come anyway!

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:21.180
After all, he...

00:03:21.180 --> 00:03:23.920
He has to come...

00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:26.440
Sara... what did you-

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:34.160
Because... because he made
a very serious promise...

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:37.130
That's why... that's why he'll...

00:03:38.500 --> 00:03:41.270
Beginning third deceleration momentarily.

00:03:41.270 --> 00:03:42.740
Countdown.

00:03:42.740 --> 00:03:44.670
Three. Two.

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:45.800
One.

00:03:51.010 --> 00:03:53.280
Brother!

00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:54.940
I'm fine...

00:03:57.850 --> 00:04:03.990
Sara, tell us everything
you saw and learned.

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:09.990
It happened over 600 years ago...

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:19.100
The spaceship belonged to neither
the Union nor the Deague.

00:04:20.540 --> 00:04:26.040
It landed on the Union resource
satellite of Nieren 6...

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:34.390
They were aliens all with the same face?!

00:04:34.390 --> 00:04:38.130
They were called UKs: "Unknowns,"

00:04:38.130 --> 00:04:40.460
and placed under military supervision.

00:04:40.460 --> 00:04:44.330
And then... research began
there in absolute secrecy...

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:56.010
Unforgivable...

00:04:56.010 --> 00:05:00.950
What they learned was that all
the girls shared some of their senses.

00:05:00.950 --> 00:05:01.920
Shared?

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:04.950
Sight, hearing, and emotion...

00:05:04.950 --> 00:05:07.590
By "all," do you mean...

00:05:07.590 --> 00:05:12.360
Even light-years apart, they can
share these, without any time lag.

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:15.260
That could have applications
in all sorts of fields!

00:05:15.260 --> 00:05:18.330
Instant interstellar communication
technology, for example!

00:05:18.330 --> 00:05:21.640
But it was for that very research...

00:05:21.640 --> 00:05:24.540
...that all those girls were...

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:29.340
I'm sorry...

00:05:30.510 --> 00:05:36.190
So that Mimic... Emily... was one of them?

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:41.060
But we have yet to realize instant
interstellar communication!

00:05:41.060 --> 00:05:42.890
What happened?

00:05:42.890 --> 00:05:46.530
As Nieren 6 wasn't originally
a research facility,

00:05:46.530 --> 00:05:49.600
technology development
could only go so far.

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:53.540
So they decided to move
the base to Planet Grabera...

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:59.000
It'd be far from the front lines,
and perfect for doing stuff in secret...

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:07.170
But, immediately after...

00:06:13.890 --> 00:06:15.220
What the-

00:06:15.220 --> 00:06:17.560
Baxter Gate?

00:06:17.560 --> 00:06:20.900
A gate that connects distant
locations in space...

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:23.360
And out of it came...

00:06:28.670 --> 00:06:31.430
To retrieve their comrades...

00:06:35.110 --> 00:06:39.180
A sub-light speed battle in
an era without Strains...

00:06:39.180 --> 00:06:41.410
Running would've been the only option...

00:06:45.920 --> 00:06:49.360
But there would be
one way to survive...

00:06:49.360 --> 00:06:51.960
Send part of the research
results to Grabera

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:54.830
and create a weapon to defeat
the enemy based on that.

00:06:54.830 --> 00:06:57.000
Yeah! A few hours of
sub-light speed travel

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:59.770
would equate to centuries
of objective time!

00:06:59.770 --> 00:07:03.410
If things go well, reinforcements
could arrive in mere minutes...

00:07:03.410 --> 00:07:06.940
So, you're saying that's why
Strains were developed?!

00:07:06.940 --> 00:07:08.280
Yes...

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:13.870
And then he... Ralph Werec...
was sent out to defeat the UKs...

00:07:15.120 --> 00:07:18.250
My brother didn't know anything...

00:07:18.250 --> 00:07:20.890
He wasn't told anything...

00:07:20.890 --> 00:07:25.330
So, he believed they were
unmanned Deague weapons...

00:07:26.930 --> 00:07:30.200
It was only after my brother
destroyed the last mobile weapon

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:32.460
that he learned the truth...

00:07:47.150 --> 00:07:50.150
Hold on a minute!
Something's not right about this!

00:07:50.150 --> 00:07:53.690
Ralph left Grabera in 7003 S.E.!

00:07:53.690 --> 00:07:56.990
Which means he should still be
traveling at sub-light speed now!

00:07:56.990 --> 00:07:59.260
He still hasn't even caught up to
the target auxiliary vessel yet!

00:07:59.260 --> 00:08:00.930
Now that you mention it...

00:08:00.930 --> 00:08:06.370
That's right. My brother caught
up with the target in 7564 S.E.

00:08:06.370 --> 00:08:10.440
Then how did Ralph show up here?!
He couldn't have!

00:08:10.440 --> 00:08:14.600
The last girl my brother
defeated opened a gate then...

00:08:16.210 --> 00:08:21.620
But isn't that for instant
transportation through space, not time?

00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:30.560
I get it! Multiple times exist
when traveling at sub-light speed!

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:34.660
So she chose Ralph's subjective
time of 7005!

00:08:37.970 --> 00:08:42.940
That would mean the gate connected
with space in 7005, right?!

00:08:42.940 --> 00:08:43.930
Yeah.

00:08:46.510 --> 00:08:49.710
And thus Ralph Werec returned?

00:08:49.710 --> 00:08:52.710
This is what happened?

00:08:52.710 --> 00:08:55.720
It's very hard to believe, but...

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:59.920
When it happened, their memories...
their feelings...

00:08:59.920 --> 00:09:03.650
They all flowed straight
into my brother...

00:09:25.950 --> 00:09:28.970
That's why my brother will come...

00:09:30.150 --> 00:09:31.980
Without fail.

00:09:41.830 --> 00:09:45.230
Final deceleration complete.
Target confirmed.

00:09:46.670 --> 00:09:50.370
Have I outlived my usefulness now?
Are you going to kill me?

00:09:53.340 --> 00:09:57.900
Hey, let me go to the bathroom.
That's not too much to ask, is it?

00:10:01.450 --> 00:10:03.440
You're so nice.

00:10:13.400 --> 00:10:15.900
What is this man thinking?

00:10:15.900 --> 00:10:18.300
If I knew this was going
to happen, I wouldn't have-

00:10:23.470 --> 00:10:25.810
An old model Union ship?

00:10:25.810 --> 00:10:28.480
How did it come
this far in that condition?

00:10:28.480 --> 00:10:31.150
We have video from
a reconnaissance TUMOR.

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:32.340
Excellent.

00:10:36.250 --> 00:10:38.350
A survivor?!

00:10:38.350 --> 00:10:42.890
I wish to defect... Iet me
speak with your commander...

00:10:42.890 --> 00:10:45.360
I wish to defect... Iet me
speak with your commander...

00:10:45.360 --> 00:10:50.090
I am Ralph Werec, a Union Reasoner.

00:10:51.700 --> 00:10:52.930
What do you think?

00:10:52.930 --> 00:10:57.110
I have a hard time believing in instant
interstellar communication,

00:10:57.110 --> 00:10:59.110
but there's a chance it is real.

00:10:59.110 --> 00:11:02.110
If we can obtain it, then I believe
we should give it a try.

00:11:02.110 --> 00:11:03.610
Indeed.

00:11:03.610 --> 00:11:05.780
If we returned home now,

00:11:05.780 --> 00:11:08.720
we would have three years
until the next operation.

00:11:08.720 --> 00:11:11.590
And I hardly doubt they would
give us a full vacation.

00:11:11.590 --> 00:11:14.620
So you choose possibly gaining glory, then?

00:11:14.620 --> 00:11:16.780
That sounds good to me...

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:23.060
You need one more?

00:11:23.060 --> 00:11:26.070
I thought you said we could use this one

00:11:26.070 --> 00:11:28.070
to develop instant
interstellar communication?

00:11:28.070 --> 00:11:31.610
To communicate, a sender
and a receiver are needed.

00:11:31.610 --> 00:11:34.910
One other exists that will parallel her.

00:11:34.910 --> 00:11:37.880
She wishes for it, as well.

00:11:37.880 --> 00:11:40.950
In parallel, huh...

00:11:40.950 --> 00:11:45.280
We've come this far, we might as well
see it through to the end.

00:11:47.690 --> 00:11:49.220
Those eyes...

00:11:49.220 --> 00:11:52.130
Those eyes are what made me-

00:11:52.130 --> 00:11:56.500
Damn it! I was a fool
to have let this man-

00:12:14.920 --> 00:12:16.820
Your ID has not been authenticated.

00:12:16.820 --> 00:12:20.560
Urgh! This is my ship!

00:12:20.560 --> 00:12:23.790
Your ID has not been authenticated.

00:12:23.790 --> 00:12:26.930
Admittance into this section is forbidden.

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:28.520
Come with me!

00:12:37.610 --> 00:12:40.010
I never thought I would have to use this...

00:12:43.210 --> 00:12:45.480
Self-destruct mechanism has been activated.

00:12:45.480 --> 00:12:48.020
--All hands, evacuate immediately.
--Let's go!

00:12:48.020 --> 00:12:50.150
Self-destruct mechanism has been activated.

00:12:50.150 --> 00:12:51.650
--All hands, evacuate immediately.

00:12:51.650 --> 00:12:54.720
--No! Brother!
--All hands, evacuate immediately.

00:12:54.720 --> 00:12:58.230
This ship is about to explode!
We have to escape!

00:12:58.230 --> 00:13:02.030
Brother! Brother!

00:13:02.030 --> 00:13:05.970
Your "brother" has gone crazy!
Surely even you can tell that!

00:13:05.970 --> 00:13:08.440
He doesn't know who's on his side or not!

00:13:08.440 --> 00:13:12.500
I wouldn't be surprised if he attacked
his own flesh and blood now!

00:13:30.630 --> 00:13:35.300
What's driving my brother now
is an intense feeling of guilt

00:13:35.300 --> 00:13:39.600
and the sense of duty that he
needs to save their survivors...

00:13:39.600 --> 00:13:44.070
He'll do whatever it takes.
He has no allies or enemies.

00:13:44.070 --> 00:13:48.710
So this ship was attacked
because she was on it, then?

00:13:48.710 --> 00:13:53.010
They would know she was here,
given that they have one, too.

00:13:53.010 --> 00:13:55.380
But, it's just the brain now!

00:13:55.380 --> 00:13:58.020
My brother probably doesn't know that.

00:13:58.020 --> 00:14:01.020
Does that mean this ship'll be
safe if we hand Emily over?!

00:14:01.020 --> 00:14:02.320
It belongs to me!

00:14:02.320 --> 00:14:04.220
Shut up, Melchi!

00:14:05.730 --> 00:14:11.570
I told you, my brother is driven
by an intense feeling of guilt...

00:14:11.570 --> 00:14:16.100
He despises all of mankind for
the terrible things they did to them.

00:14:16.100 --> 00:14:21.170
In my brother's eyes, all humans
must be killed for vengeance.

00:14:23.650 --> 00:14:26.080
I take it you heard?

00:14:26.080 --> 00:14:27.740
Queen...

00:14:33.520 --> 00:14:36.220
I heard, but it doesn't-

00:14:36.220 --> 00:14:39.220
That doesn't mean that Carris had to-

00:14:42.800 --> 00:14:45.070
W-what?! An enemy attack?!

00:14:45.070 --> 00:14:46.430
Let's go!

00:14:46.430 --> 00:14:47.590
Y-yeah!

00:14:49.840 --> 00:14:51.070
A shuttle?!

00:14:51.070 --> 00:14:55.280
Yes, sir! It's sending
a distress signal and closing in!

00:14:55.280 --> 00:14:59.280
It's not even 3 light-seconds away!
Why didn't you notice sooner?!

00:14:59.280 --> 00:15:03.020
We weren't able to repair
the sensors at Gall...

00:15:03.020 --> 00:15:05.950
A message from the shuttle!

00:15:05.950 --> 00:15:07.620
They say they surrender!

00:15:07.620 --> 00:15:08.820
Surrender?

00:15:08.820 --> 00:15:13.860
The sender is Vivian Medlock,
captain of the Deague ship Kunrun!

00:15:13.860 --> 00:15:16.900
--A Deague captain?!
--Why would she surrender?!

00:15:16.900 --> 00:15:18.970
Can we speak directly?

00:15:18.970 --> 00:15:20.970
Yes, sir!

00:15:20.970 --> 00:15:26.210
This is Craven, current head of
the Union exercise ship Libertad.

00:15:26.210 --> 00:15:28.680
I'll save you the details for later.

00:15:28.680 --> 00:15:30.650
For now, I request protection
aboard your ship.

00:15:30.650 --> 00:15:34.320
Just what has happened,
Captain Medlock?!

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:38.480
I was betrayed by Ralph Werec!
So I fled here!

00:15:42.090 --> 00:15:44.560
He's gone insane!

00:15:44.560 --> 00:15:48.430
He murdered all of my crew
and took control of the ship!

00:15:48.430 --> 00:15:51.700
All to get the "other one" that you have!

00:15:53.070 --> 00:15:54.500
"Other one"?

00:15:54.500 --> 00:15:57.670
It matches with Sara Werec's story...

00:15:57.670 --> 00:15:59.910
As long as you'll guarantee my life,

00:15:59.910 --> 00:16:03.210
I'll return the sample we stole
from the Grabera laboratory.

00:16:03.210 --> 00:16:04.510
Captain Medlock.

00:16:04.510 --> 00:16:05.710
If we agree to that,

00:16:05.710 --> 00:16:10.090
Ralph Werec will come after us
even more fiercely than before.

00:16:10.090 --> 00:16:12.850
There's no need to worry about that.

00:16:12.850 --> 00:16:15.190
The Kunrun will self-destruct very soon!

00:16:29.740 --> 00:16:32.410
Hey. Are all Deague soldiers like that?

00:16:32.410 --> 00:16:33.710
Of course not...

00:16:33.710 --> 00:16:36.610
Their physical checkups
must be easy, though...

00:16:36.610 --> 00:16:41.150
Hey, girls! Does the Union always
keep captured officers naked?!

00:16:41.150 --> 00:16:42.950
Go bring me some clothes!

00:16:43.990 --> 00:16:46.580
So she's Emily...

00:16:48.090 --> 00:16:49.720
Enemy ship detected!

00:16:49.720 --> 00:16:52.630
It's closing in on us!
It's a collision course!

00:16:52.630 --> 00:16:55.000
He's trying to take us with him?!

00:16:55.000 --> 00:16:57.370
Can we shake him off
with emergency acceleration?!

00:16:57.370 --> 00:17:01.840
Mercurion level rising! 3 minutes
40 seconds to acceleration!

00:17:01.840 --> 00:17:03.830
He's going to catch up to us!

00:17:05.370 --> 00:17:07.910
All hands to battle stations!

00:17:07.910 --> 00:17:10.640
Destroy the approaching enemy ship!

00:17:12.510 --> 00:17:15.920
Sara. You still haven't
been permitted to fight.

00:17:15.920 --> 00:17:21.220
But if Ralph Werec is coming,
I think it's your duty to fight him.

00:17:21.220 --> 00:17:22.420
Yes.

00:17:23.560 --> 00:17:25.650
We'll go get things ready.

00:17:29.960 --> 00:17:34.970
Course projection shows it
coming at us in a suicide attack.

00:17:34.970 --> 00:17:37.560
We must keep it away at all costs!

00:17:38.770 --> 00:17:41.240
I'm amazed she can sleep
at a time like this...

00:17:44.010 --> 00:17:46.080
Dammit! I gotta stay behind?!

00:17:46.080 --> 00:17:50.620
Don't complain! Just leave this
to us, and do what you can do!

00:17:50.620 --> 00:17:52.750
Got it, Dickon?!

00:17:54.120 --> 00:17:58.330
Yeah! I'm stuck like this,
but you can count on me!

00:17:58.330 --> 00:17:59.660
Thanks!

00:18:00.800 --> 00:18:04.630
Prepare for evasive maneuvers!
How do the engines look?!

00:18:04.630 --> 00:18:07.540
Output increasing for all sub
and auxiliary engines!

00:18:07.540 --> 00:18:10.030
110 to main engine drive!

00:18:33.390 --> 00:18:35.560
Gambee E01, to launch position!

00:18:35.560 --> 00:18:36.550
Roger.

00:18:43.640 --> 00:18:45.970
All units! Don't stray
too far from the Libertad!

00:18:45.970 --> 00:18:47.570
You'll get left behind!

00:18:52.310 --> 00:18:54.320
Only five in all...

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:57.690
The Spatial Armor Division
sure has gotten lonely, too...

00:18:57.690 --> 00:19:00.420
Lottie. If that Gloire shows
up with us like this...

00:19:00.420 --> 00:19:02.420
I know.

00:19:02.420 --> 00:19:04.430
Bridge! Do you read me?

00:19:04.430 --> 00:19:08.860
Send out Gutsy Girl!
Send out Sara Werec! We need her!

00:19:08.860 --> 00:19:11.470
We need her help to stop the Deague ship!

00:19:11.470 --> 00:19:14.340
Send out Gutsy Girl's Strain!

00:19:14.340 --> 00:19:18.040
--Lottie. Are you sure?
--She's Ralph Werec's-

00:19:18.040 --> 00:19:21.610
So what? It doesn't matter
whose sister she is!

00:19:21.610 --> 00:19:24.750
Sara's a member of the
Spatial Armor Division now!

00:19:24.750 --> 00:19:27.480
She's a friend we can entrust our lives to!

00:19:27.480 --> 00:19:29.610
Lottie-san...

00:19:30.950 --> 00:19:32.720
In that case...

00:19:34.360 --> 00:19:36.890
Alright, Queen!

00:19:36.890 --> 00:19:41.330
Then let's try hard while we wait
for Sara-san to come! Okay?

00:19:42.360 --> 00:19:45.670
You heard the ladies, Bridge!

00:19:45.670 --> 00:19:46.970
Understood.

00:19:46.970 --> 00:19:49.990
Strain EX! Prepare to launch!

00:19:54.740 --> 00:19:56.480
We made some adjustments.

00:19:56.480 --> 00:19:59.050
There shouldn't be any more
link malfunctions like before.

00:19:59.050 --> 00:20:01.080
Here you go!

00:20:01.080 --> 00:20:02.550
Thank you.

00:20:15.830 --> 00:20:17.100
Brother...

00:20:17.100 --> 00:20:21.670
I've learned what you saw...
what you felt...

00:20:21.670 --> 00:20:26.010
But, even so, I will stop you!

00:20:26.010 --> 00:20:27.500
No matter what it takes!

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:36.400
The brother before me now is
no longer the brother from that day.

00:20:36.400 --> 00:20:40.770
On the next Soukou no Strain:
"Attack on the Libertad"

00:20:40.770 --> 00:20:43.100
Brother... Let's put an end to this.
